  "goodToKnow": "Duften means to smell pleasantly: Der Kuchen duftet herrlich, Es duftet nach Zimt. For neutral smelling Germans say riechen, and for bad smells stinken. Der Duft is a scent or fragrance: der Duft von frischem Brot. Casually, dufte was Berlin slang for great or terrific, now old-fashioned: Das ist ja dufte! The word comes from an old word for mist or vapour, the way a scent spreads through the air."
